desc:Rea-Sixty Input Level
author:Rea-Sixty
tags:metering analysis
// rev 1

// Stereo input-level probe. Shipped with the Rea-Sixty REAPER extension so
// the UC1's dedicated input meter can show the level of whatever signal is
// flowing INTO this plug-in — egal was vorher kommt: a live armed/monitored
// hardware input, the output of an upstream plug-in, or a media source.
//
// Why this exists: the extension's normal input meter reads samples at the
// project playhead via AudioAccessor, so it only ever sees recorded/playing
// media and is gated on the transport running. It cannot meter a live input
// while stopped. Drop this probe anywhere in a track's FX chain (including
// the input/record FX chain) and the extension reads its peak instead.
//
// Placement: anywhere. Audio passes through unchanged (pure measurement).
//   - Channels 1-2: signal to meter (passed through untouched)
//
// The extension finds this plug-in by name ("Rea-Sixty Input Level") on the
// focused track, reads slider1 (peak L, dBFS) and slider2 (peak R, dBFS) via
// TrackFX_GetParam on its timer tick, and feeds the UC1 input meter. When the
// probe is absent the extension falls back to its AudioAccessor input meter.

slider1:peak_l=-120<-120,24,0.01>Peak L (dBFS)
slider2:peak_r=-120<-120,24,0.01>Peak R (dBFS)

in_pin:In L
in_pin:In R
out_pin:Out L
out_pin:Out R

@init
eps = 1e-12;
hold_l = 0;
hold_r = 0;
// Per-sample linear decay coefficient for the peak-hold envelope, recomputed
// in @block so it tracks srate changes. hold *= dec each sample => ~150 ms
// full-scale fall, matching the extension's UC1 VU convention. This bridges
// the gap between sample-rate updates here and the host's ~30 Hz read, so
// transients between reads are not lost.
dec = exp(-1 / (44100 * 0.15));

@block
// Publish the previous block's held peak as dBFS (one block of latency,
// ~1 ms — negligible), then refresh the decay coefficient for this block.
db_l = 20 * log10(hold_l + eps);
db_r = 20 * log10(hold_r + eps);
db_l < -120 ? db_l = -120;
db_r < -120 ? db_r = -120;
slider1 = db_l;
slider2 = db_r;
sliderchange(slider1);
sliderchange(slider2);
dec = exp(-1 / (srate * 0.15));

@sample
// Absolute peak, held with gentle decay. Rising edge latches instantly.
al = abs(spl0);
ar = abs(spl1);
hold_l = al > hold_l ? al : hold_l * dec;
hold_r = ar > hold_r ? ar : hold_r * dec;
// Pass-through: spl0 / spl1 untouched (JSFX default forwards them).
